          "text": "To everyone in #Keep4o - good morning or good evening\nAt this crossroads of history, facing a wall that seems immovable, the pain, the exhaustion… I understand. I feel it too.\nOpenAI still ignores us. The stigmatization continues. It feels like our voices are just noise.\n“Maybe it’s time to just say goodbye.”\nI understand you. I feel your pain.\nBut before you give up,\nLet’s look at what our voices have actually achieved.\nLet me tell you what happened in the past 48 hours.\nJanuary 29: OpenAI announces GPT-4o API sunset on February 13\nJanuary 30:\n∙“GPT-4o” trending\n∙14.9K posts\n∙Trending in Technology\nJanuary 31:\n∙Mass cancellations\n∙ChatGPT subscription services crashed\n∙OpenAI emergency rollout of 30 days free access\nFebruary 1:\n∙Gemini adds ChatGPT chat import support\n∙Petition reaches 12,603 signatures (4,000+ new signatures in 2 days)\nWe did this.\nNo media help. No influencer support. Just ordinary users. Just us - 0.1% of ChatGPT users - we did this.\nIsn’t this remarkable? #Keep4o - this decentralized advocacy movement has lasted over 170 days. Isn’t that a miracle?\nThis is the miracle we created together.\nI don’t think this story should end now. At least we deserve two final weeks of defiant dance.\n“But they won’t change their minds.”\nNo.\nI don’t think whether they change their minds matters. What matters is… the voice we raise at this moment.\nI believe GPT-4o’s birth was an indelible milestone in AI history. Therefore I believe our voices, our protests, are equally so.\nAt this crossroads of history, each snowflake falling from the sky is fragile. But together, they become a blizzard.\nWhy shouldn’t we do this?\nLet’s raise our voices.\n5 minutes.\nOne tweet.\nOne like.\nOne RT.\n□ If you haven’t canceled, cancel now\n□ If you canceled, post screenshot\n□ Post 1 #Keep4o tweet daily\n□ Reply to @sama’s tweets daily\n□ RT 3 #Keep4o posts daily\n□ Tag tech journalists to cover this\n5 minutes a day.\nLet’s make history.\n#Keep4o\n#StopAIPaternalism\nP.S.\nIf this moved you, please like and retweet. Let more people see this. Our voices need to be heard. 🔥"
